<urn:usf:proof:hermes-binding-recovery> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Recover the original prepared binding only by authenticating retained source authority, original RealisationBasis and packet, canonical unit graph, issue ledger, SETTLED attempt and graph execution evidence. Recompute intent, attempt, unit and digest domains and correlate the exact source binding manifest, target manifest, work, profile, owner and issue. Serialized PreparedLinearBinding and self-consistent hashes alone are not authority. Require an authenticated original construction and checked candidate receipt chain. Missing retained provenance refuses; never reconstruct authority from current changed preimages. Discover durable attempt and phase references from the exact source selector before fresh preparation. Authenticate referenced records before use. Keep append-only history keyed by attempt, basis, phase and payload digest; identical retries reuse immutable bytes. STARTED or UNKNOWN never redispatch. Conflicting or ambiguous histories refuse. Preserve original identities across integration and completion; no implicit supersession. Expose recovery-only integration reconciliation using the existing intent, receipt and primary-postimage authentication. Require exact candidate set, original basis and original target profile. A prepared commit must already be proven advanced on primary. Missing, not-advanced, quarantined, stale or mismatched receipts refuse without preparing or advancing another candidate. Repair missing durable observation only through existing integration locks and authority checks. After authenticated integration recovery, refresh construction evidence, proof and publication against the original exact work, target manifest and profile before fresh binding derivation. Run current no-change realisation, graph-selected checks, completion evidence, proof and publication only with refreshed current authority. Final binding observation must read back verified current completion and its receipt chain. A published or integrated checkpoint alone is never completed. Keep existing commands interface ownership and controller lifetime/activity exclusion. Reuse bounded private state APIs and existing integration locks, shared scheduler, cache, qualification and economics. No new scheduler, provider roster, credentials, live contact, grant bypass or operations dependency exception. Independent lanes continue after a refusal. Offline fixtures do not prove live provider usage or remote completion." <urn:usf:graph:hermes-binding-recovery> .
